{
  "label": "Deck Handling Board",
  "order": 1,
  "$description": "The carrier \"Ouija board\": a top-down deck plan where handlers move aircraft templates. Agents are craft parked in deck zones; each Round is a cut template in its holder, numbered by its deck spot, set in drafting lettering. Craft geometry carries the identity, not hazard paint.",
  "signature": "When a Round is answered, its own strip departs: while the core holds it in .hh-strip[data-state=\"departing\"], the craft on the template taxis along a catapult track drawn across the strip and runs off the board, and the template clears its spot. The status word stays printed throughout; under reduced motion the strip simply clears.",
  "colorScheme": "dark",
